#part[Types]

_Types that are checked before program execution---what are known as static types---are a vital part of programming, and a growing number of languages either have them from the start or, realizing their importance, are adding them in various forms. Types are a common first step towards proving properties about programs. If you use a typed language, you write small proofs about your programs every day, whether you realize it or not._
